{"h":3396,"lines":[{"x":0.82240490078981887,"y":0.029163343093938976,"h":0.019161970230659686,"c":1,"w":0.085622800191243464,"t":"Reading"},{"y":0.08127208489214055,"x":0.067901238233322656,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.3086419677734375,"c":1},{"h":0.023993449441395365,"c":1,"w":0.82948633829752594,"y":0.11437327415542353,"x":0.067783034109991147,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading"},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"Passage 3 below.","w":0.17078189849853515,"c":1,"y":0.13662790682113579,"x":0.067901231696313194},{"x":0.31481481767964936,"y":0.17432273267773579,"h":0.017667844522968212,"t":"How to make wise decisions","w":0.34362139383951829,"c":1},{"w":0.82729115804036468,"y":0.21072915735184683,"x":0.067839654552898684,"h":0.019228674638116838,"c":1,"t":"Across cultures, wisdom has been considered one of the most revered human qualities. Although"},{"t":"the truly wise may seem few and far between, empirical rescarch examining wisdom suggests","w":0.80452672322591146,"x":0.065843639750212901,"h":0.018895348053517669,"y":0.22819767457425866,"c":1},{"t":"that it isn't an exceptional trait possessed by a small handful of bearded philosophers after all - in","w":0.8376372782389323,"h":0.020951802373915362,"c":1,"x":0.06575407424239757,"y":0.24601754166095013},{"h":0.020612485276796266,"t":"fact, the latest studies suggest that most of us have the ability to make wise decisions, given the","x":0.065843639116411806,"w":0.81687240600585942,"c":1,"y":0.26295641981867746},{"w":0.11737155914306642,"x":0.067857429583965109,"c":1,"t":"right context.","y":0.28615870119110975,"h":0.014891899657052843},{"t":"'It appears that experiential, situational, and cultural factors are even more powerful in shaping","w":0.81292556762695312,"x":0.067839447533040984,"h":0.020885168733810189,"y":0.31777289051074642,"c":1},{"y":0.33348493959879111,"t":"wisdom than previously imagined,' says Associate Professor Igor Grossmann of the University","c":1,"w":0.80681950887044285,"h":0.022074448907894784,"x":0.067784066637658402},{"c":1,"x":0.067726563265908146,"t":"of Waterloo in Ontario, Canada. 'Recent empirical findings from cognitive, developmental,","h":0.024125262059367936,"w":0.78013142903645827,"y":0.35072020226351142},{"h":0.022879651073011043,"y":0.36934379885475765,"c":1,"x":0.067752777134395981,"t":"social, and personality psychology cumulatively suggest that people's ability to reason wisely","w":0.79866724650065091},{"c":1,"y":0.38910105289597152,"t":"varies dramatically across experiential and situational contexts. Understanding the role of such","x":0.067815891797597672,"w":0.81088389078776046,"h":0.018786738702349481},{"x":0.067794499376370443,"w":0.83971018473307302,"h":0.021115227779033519,"y":0.40598661582552931,"t":"contextual factors offers unique insights into understanding wisdom in daily life, as well as how it","c":1},{"y":0.4241585038466269,"h":0.023857918729209282,"t":"can be enhanced and taught.?","w":0.25426066080729165,"x":0.067439311225021989,"c":1},{"x":0.067785211345214022,"w":0.79862345377604171,"t":"It seems that it's not so much that some people simply possess wisdom and others lack it, but","y":0.45912669946713391,"c":1,"h":0.021074971265309772},{"x":0.067817268075863246,"c":1,"w":0.78618682861328115,"y":0.47703347373764093,"h":0.019747393712559291,"t":"that our ability to reason wisely depends on a variety of external factors. 'It is impossible to"},{"h":0.020742369203601285,"w":0.81094106038411451,"c":1,"t":"characterize thought processes attributed to wisdom without considering the role of contextual","y":0.49517074695451824,"x":0.067797928149687631},{"h":0.023539064629760298,"c":1,"x":0.067761504454829077,"y":0.51104769033733644,"w":0.82540669759114582,"t":"factors,' explains Grossmann. 'In other words, wisdom is not solely an \"inner quality\" but rather"},{"c":1,"h":0.020259792026838697,"w":0.79239435831705729,"y":0.53071718236192,"t":"unfolds as a function of situations people happen to be in. Some situations are more likely to","x":0.069847674131472109},{"y":0.54919026119708192,"w":0.26032292683919267,"h":0.020767299530784156,"c":1,"x":0.069426300048541806,"t":"promote wisdom than others.'"},{"x":0.069864940264925221,"t":"Coming up with a definition of wisdom is challenging, but Grossmann and his colleagues have","y":0.58360767730859964,"w":0.81294255574544261,"h":0.019965206635995325,"c":1},{"h":0.020512883036942653,"c":1,"t":"identified four key characteristics as part of a framework of wise reasoning. One is intellectual","w":0.81092814127604163,"x":0.067796694705325247,"y":0.60142398226327998},{"x":0.069879330592117511,"t":"humility or recognition of the limits of our own knowledge, and another is appreciation of","y":0.62015288526256751,"w":0.77385630289713547,"c":1,"h":0.020997587727433209},{"c":1,"t":"perspectives wider than the issue at hand. Sensitivity to the possibility of change in social","w":0.76768458048502608,"x":0.069861259564866315,"y":0.63783811499713261,"h":0.020789360971978699},{"x":0.069840913544072306,"h":0.021614306105039782,"c":1,"t":"relations is also key, along with compromise or integration of different attitudes and beliefs.","y":0.65501714100974773,"w":0.78623316446940106},{"x":0.07194357180131912,"y":0.69104293468579781,"h":0.018895237970969925,"c":1,"w":0.78615300496419271,"t":"Grossmann and his colleagues have also found that one of the most reliable ways to support"},{"x":0.072016461921641059,"c":1,"t":"wisdom in our own day-to-day decisions is to look at scenarios from a third-party perspective, as","h":0.017441860778592888,"y":0.70930232541794869,"w":0.82716049194335939},{"h":0.019929223122388873,"t":"though giving advice to a friend. Research suggests that when adopting a first-person viewpoint","w":0.82115051269531258,"c":1,"x":0.069884815650083185,"y":0.72605883627313028},{"c":1,"x":0.071846114607233835,"w":0.83167088826497415,"t":"we focus on 'the focal features of the environment' and when we adopt a third-person, 'observer'","y":0.74120356858941294,"h":0.024935586432826451},{"h":0.021652245268804826,"c":1,"t":"viewpoint we reason more broadly and focus more on interpersonal and moral ideals such as","y":0.76081597139255963,"x":0.069825547129720847,"w":0.79655863444010411},{"x":0.067787664015841353,"h":0.020303265646854807,"w":0.79650121053059908,"t":"justice and impartiality. Looking at problems from this more expansive viewpoint appears to","y":0.77915642014769293,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.80087209287431971,"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.069958838862301503,"w":0.44650207519531249,"t":"foster cognitive processes related to wise decisions."},{"c":1,"y":0.9055232556460866,"t":"47","h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.88477366207572405,"w":0.026748971939086874}],"w":2400}